Hi Sharon,
You can still call optmatch from MatchIt to run optimal matching; just ignore that warning.  (See sample code and output below).

It sounds like you're running it from within an R GUI, which may cause trouble with optmatch; I'm not sure.  But I was able to get the code below to run fine.

Thanks,
Liz

> library(MatchIt)
Loading required package: MASS
##
##  MatchIt (Version 2.4-20, built: 2011-10-24)
##  Please refer to http://gking.harvard.edu/matchit for full documentation
##  or help.matchit() for help with commands supported by MatchIt.
##
> data(lalonde)
> m.out <- matchit(treat ~ age + educ + re74 + re75, data=lalonde, method="optimal")
Loading required package: optmatch
